				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
							<p>The six cognitive types—Analytical, Creative, Realistic, Practical, Protective, and Strategic—are not tied to specific brain structures but serve as a metaphorical framework to understand how individuals think, process information, and face challenges. Rooted in observable patterns of behavior and cognitive tendencies, this model highlights the brain’s dynamic and integrated nature.</p><p>Rather than isolating traits to single brain regions, these types reflect how different areas interact to shape unique strengths and growth opportunities. By embracing this framework, individuals can uncover their natural tendencies, harness their strengths, and navigate personal development with clarity and purpose.</p>						</div>
